opment tools; JRE contains JVM plus core libraries','JVM contains JDK and JRE','JRE is used only for compiling .java files','JDK is platform-independent bytecode','A'),(502,21,'Which of the following accurately describes Method Overloading vs Method Overriding in Java?','Overloading is compile-time (same name, different parameters); Overriding is runtime in a subclass','Overloading requires inheritance; Overriding happens in the same class','Static methods can be overridden at runtime','Constructors can be overridden by subclasses','A'),(503,21,'Which of the following accurately describes Java String immutability and String Pool?','String objects cannot be modified once created; literals are cached in the String Pool','Strings are mutable character arrays like C','StringBuilder is immutable and thread-safe','The == operator always compares String contents','A'),(504,21,'Which of the following accurately describes == operator vs .equals() method in Java?','== compares object references (memory addresses); .equals() compares logical content','== compares String characters; .equals() compares memory addresses','They behave identically for all objects','.equals() works only on primitive int types','A'),(505,21,'Which of the following accurately describes Abstract Class vs Interface in Java (JDK 8+)?','A class can extend only one abstract class but implement multiple interfaces','Interfaces can have instance fields and constructors','Abstract classes cannot have concrete methods','Interfaces cannot have default or static methods','A'),(506,21,'Which of the following accurately describes final keyword in Java (variable, method, class)?','final variable is constant; final method cannot be overridden; final class cannot be subclassed','final class cannot be instantiated','final method cannot be called','final variable is automatically garbage collected','A'),(507,21,'Which of the following accurately describes Checked vs Unchecked Exceptions in Java?','Checked exceptions (e.g., IOException) are verified at compile time; Unchecked extend RuntimeException','NullPointerException is a checked exception','Error subclasses must be caught in every method','Unchecked exceptions require a throws clause','A'),(508,21,'Which of the following accurately describes try-with-resources statement in Java?','Automatically closes any resource implementing AutoCloseable at the end of the block','Suppresses all syntax errors at compile time','Replaces the JVM garbage collector','Runs only when an exception is thrown','A'),(509,21,'Which of the following accurately describes HashMap internal working in Java 8+?','Uses an array of buckets (hashCode & equals) and converts long collision chains to balanced trees','Stores keys in sorted ascending order','Allows multiple duplicate keys','Is fully synchronized by default','A'),(510,21,'Which of the following accurately describes ArrayList vs LinkedList in Java Collections?','ArrayList uses a dynamic array with O(1) random access; LinkedList uses doubly-linked nodes','LinkedList has O(1) random access by index','ArrayList uses more memory per element than LinkedList','ArrayList implements the Queue interface directly','A'),(511,21,'Which of the following accurately describes HashSet vs TreeSet in Java?','HashSet is backed by a HashMap (O(1) lookup, unordered); TreeSet uses a Red-Black Tree (O(log n), sorted)','HashSet maintains insertion order','TreeSet allows multiple null elements','HashSet requires elements to implement Comparable','A'),(512,21,'Which of the following accurately describes Comparable vs Comparator interfaces in Java?','Comparable defines natural ordering via compareTo(); Comparator defines custom external ordering via compare()','Comparable is in java.util and takes two arguments','Comparator modifies the original class source code','Only one Comparator can exist per class','A'),(513,21,'Which of the following accurately describes synchronized keyword in Java multithreading?','Acquires an intri