ches','Boundary Value Analysis is a white-box technique','Black-box tests specifications without internal code view (ECP, BVA); White-box tests internal code paths','Statement coverage is a black-box metric','C'),(809,33,'When analyzing system design and implementation, which statement holds true regarding Boundary Value Analysis (BVA) and Equivalence Partitioning?','Tests every possible 64-bit integer exhaustively','Tests only internal private methods','Tests input domain partition boundaries (min, min-1, min+1, max, max-1, max+1) where defects cluster','Replaces integration testing','C'),(810,33,'When analyzing system design and implementation, which statement holds true regarding Unit, Integration, System, and Acceptance Testing order?','Acceptance -> System -> Integration -> Unit','System -> Unit -> Acceptance -> Integration','Unit -> Integration -> System -> Acceptance (Alpha/Beta/UAT)','Integration -> Unit -> System -> Acceptance','C'),(811,33,'When analyzing system design and implementation, which statement holds true regarding Regression Testing purpose?','Tests only brand-new features for the first time','Measures server network bandwidth','Verifies that recent code changes or bug fixes have not broken existing working functionality','Generates UML diagrams from requirements','C'),(812,33,'When analyzing system design and implementation, which statement holds true regarding Alpha Testing vs Beta Testing?','Alpha is performed after production release by anonymous users','Beta is performed by the compiler','Alpha is performed at the developer\'s site in a controlled environment; Beta is performed by real users at their site','Both are white-box unit tests','C'),(813,33,'When analyzing system design and implementation, which statement holds true regarding Singleton, Factory, and Observer Design Patterns (GoF)?','Singleton creates a new instance on every call','Observer is a creational pattern','Singleton: single instance; Factory: encapsulates object creation;