rder within the element\'s declared width and height','Adds margin inside the content box','Disables borders on the element','Forces the element to display inline','A'),(879,36,'Which of the following accurately describes CSS Specificity hierarchy (highest to lowest)?','Inline styles (1000) > ID selectors (100) > Class/Attribute/Pseudo-class (10) > Element/Type (1)','Element selectors override ID selectors','Class selectors override inline styles','Universal selector (*) has the highest specificity','A'),(880,36,'Which of the following accurately describes CSS Flexbox vs CSS Grid layout?','Flexbox is designed for 1D layout (row or column); CSS Grid is designed for 2D layout (rows and columns)','Flexbox is 2D; CSS Grid is 1D only','Flexbox cannot center items vertically','CSS Grid requires external JavaScript libraries','A'),(881,36,'Which of the following accurately describes JavaScript var vs let vs const (ES6)?','let and const are block-scoped; var is function-scoped; const prevents variable reassignment','var is block-scoped','const makes object properties deeply immutable','let can be redeclared in the same block','A'),(882,36,'Which of the following accurately describes JavaScript Event Bubbling vs Event Capturing?','Bubbling propagates from target element up to document root; Capturing propagates down from root to target','Bubbling goes top-down; Capturing goes bottom-up','event.stopPropagation() triggers all parent listeners','Event delegation relies on disabling bubbling','A'),(883,36,'Which of the following accurately describes JavaScript Promises and async/await?','Represent eventual completion/failure of asynchronous operations, avoiding callback hell','Block the main browser UI thread until the network responds','Create new OS kernel threads','Can only resolve once per page reload','A'),(884,36,'Which of the following accurately describes JavaScript Event Loop, Call Stack, and Task/Microtask Queues?','Executes synchronous code on the call stack, then dra