 Backpropagation algorithm in Neural Networks?','Updates input features while keeping weights fixed','Runs only during inference on test data','Computes gradients of the loss function with respect to weights efficiently using the chain rule of calculus','Does not require differentiable activation functions','C'),(1068,43,'When analyzing system design and implementation, which statement holds true regarding Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) key operations?','Uses fully connected layers for every pixel without weight sharing','Cannot process 2D grid data like images','Uses shared-weight convolutional filters (local receptive fields) and pooling layers for spatial hierarchy','Pooling layers increase spatial resolution','C'),(1069,43,'When analyzing system design and implementation, which statement holds true regarding Cross-Validation (k-Fold Cross-Validation)?','Trains on the test set directly to maximize accuracy','Uses the same fold for both training and validation simultaneously','Partitions data into k folds, training on k-1 folds and validating on the held-out fold k times to estimate generalization','Replaces the need for a loss function','C'),(1070,43,'When analyzing system design and implementation, which statement holds true regarding Random Forest vs Gradient Boosting (XGBoost)?','Random Forest builds trees sequentially where each tree fits residuals','Gradient Boosting cannot overfit if 10,000 trees are added','Random Forest bags independent trees in parallel (reduces variance); Boosting builds sequential trees correcting prior residuals (reduces bias)','Both train only a single decision stump','C'),(1071,43,'When analyzing system design and implementation, which statement holds true regarding Naive Bayes Classifier assumption?','Assumes features are 100% linearly correlated','Requires millions of epochs of gradient descent','Assumes features are conditionally independent given the class label, applying Bayes\' Theorem','Cannot be used for text spam clas