 zero (+0 and -0)','Range for n bits is -(2^(n-1) - 1) to +(2^(n-1) - 1)','Cannot perform subtraction using an adder','Obtained by inverting all bits (1\'s complement) and adding 1; has a single representation for zero','D'),(1202,49,'Identify the valid specification or operational behavior associated with IEEE 754 Single-Precision (32-bit) Floating Point format:','1 sign bit, 11 exponent bits, and 52 mantissa bits','Uses 2\'s complement for the exponent field','Has no representation for NaN or Infinity','1 sign bit, 8 exponent bits (bias 127), and 23 fraction/mantissa bits (with implicit leading 1)','D'),(1203,49,'Identify the valid specification or operational behavior associated with Universal Logic Gates (NAND and NOR):','AND and OR are universal gates without NOT','XOR alone can implement any Boolean function without constants','NAND is equivalent to OR followed by NOT','Any Boolean function (AND, OR, NOT, XOR) can be implemented using only NAND gates or only NOR gates','D'),(1204,49,'Identify the valid specification or operational behavior associated with De Morgan\'s Theorems in Boolean Algebra:','NOT(A AND B) = (NOT A) AND (NOT B)','A + (B . C) = (A . B) + C','A XOR B = A AND B','NOT(A AND B) = (NOT A) OR (NOT B), and NOT(A OR B) = (NOT A) AND (NOT B)','D'),(1205,49,'Identify the valid specification or operational behavior associated with Combinational vs Sequential Logic Circuits:','Multiplexer is a sequential circuit with memory','JK Flip-Flop is a combinational circuit','Combinational circuits require a clock signal','Combinational output depends only on current inputs (Adder, Mux); Sequential depends on current inputs and past state (Flip-Flops)','D'),(1206,49,'Identify the valid specification or operational behavior associated with Program Counter (PC) and Instruction Register (IR):','PC holds the result of ALU addition','IR holds the stack pointer address','Both are stored on the hard disk','PC holds the memory address of the next instruction to fetch;