wired uses combinational logic/FSM (faster, RISC); Microprogrammed uses control memory storing microinstructions (flexible, CISC)','D'),(1212,49,'Identify the valid specification or operational behavior associated with 5-Stage RISC Instruction Pipeline stages:','Fetch -> Compile -> Link -> Load -> Execute','Decode -> Fetch -> Memory -> Execute -> Write Back','Pipelining reduces the latency of a single instruction to 1/5th','Instruction Fetch (IF) -> Instruction Decode (ID) -> Execute (EX) -> Memory Access (MEM) -> Write Back (WB)','D'),(1213,49,'Identify the valid specification or operational behavior associated with Structural, Data, and Control Hazards in Pipelining:','Forwarding resolves all branch control hazards','RAW (Read After Write) is a false dependency solved by register renaming','Adding more pipeline stages eliminates branch penalties','Structural: hardware resource conflict; Data: RAW/WAR/WAW dependency; Control: branch/jump instruction changes PC','D'),(1214,49,'Identify the valid specification or operational behavior associated with Operand Forwarding (Bypassing) in a Pipeline:','Eliminates the need for a load-use stall immediately after LW','Predicts branch outcomes at compile time','Writes results directly to the hard drive','Routes ALU output from EX/MEM or MEM/WB pipeline buffers directly to ALU inputs to avoid data hazard stalls','D'),(1215,49,'Identify the valid specification or operational behavior associated with Principle of Locality (Temporal and Spatial Locality):','Temporal locality justifies fetching multi-word cache lines','Spatial locality justifies keeping loop counters in registers','Random memory access exhibits maximal spatial locality','Temporal: recently accessed items likely accessed again soon; Spatial: nearby memory addresses likely accessed soon','D'),(1216,49,'Identify the valid specification or operational behavior associated with Direct-Mapped, Fully Associative, and Set-Associative Cache:','Direct-mapped cache has zero conflict misses','Fully associative cache requires no tag comparators','Set-associative cache cannot use LRU replacement','Direct-mapped: 1 block location (index = block mod N); Fully associative: any line; k-way Set-Associative: k lines per set','D'),(1217,49,'Identify the valid specification or operational behavior associated with Cache Write Policies (Write-Through vs Write-Back):','Write-Back writes to main memory on every CPU store instruction','Write-Through requires a dirty bit per cache line','Write-Back generates more memory bus traffic than Write-Through','Write-Through updates both cache and main memory on every write; Write-Back updates only cache (dirty bit) until eviction','D'),(1218,49,'Identify the valid specification or operational behavior associated with Effective Memory Access Time (EMAT) formula:','EMAT = Hit_Rate * Miss_Penalty','EMAT = Miss_Time / Hit_Rate','EMAT is independent of the miss penalty','EMAT = Hit_Time + (Miss_Rate * Miss_Penalty)','D'),(1219,49,'Identify the valid specification or operational behavior associated with Programmed I/O, Interrupt-Driven I/O, and Direct Memory Access (DMA):','Programmed I/O frees the CPU to run other processes while polling','DMA transfers data through CPU general-purpose registers on every byte','Interrupt-Driven I/O has lower overhead than DMA for 1 GB disk transfers','DMA transfers blocks directly between I/O device and memory via a DMA controller without continuous CPU intervention','D'),(1220,49,'Identify the valid specification or operational behavior associated with Endianness (Big-Endian vs Little-Endian):','Little-Endian reverses the bits inside each individual byte','Network byte order (TCP/IP) is Little-Endian','x86-64 processors are Big-Endian only','Big-Endian stores the most significant byte (MSB) at the lowest memory address; Little-Endian stores the LSB at the lowest address','D'),(1221,49,'Identify the valid specification or operational behavior associated with Amdahl\'s Law for parallel speedup:','Speedup increases linearly to infinity even if 50% of the code is serial','Doubling processors always doubles total program speed','Applies only to disk storage capacity','Speedup = 1 / ((1 - f) + (f / N)), where f is the parallelizable fraction and N is the number of processors','D'),(1222,49,'Identify the valid specification or operational behavior associated with CPU Performance Equation (Execution Time):','CPU Time = Clock Rate / (IC * CPI)','A higher clock rate (GHz) always guarantees lower CPU time regardless of CPI','CPI is always 1.0 for every instruction','CPU Time = Instruction Count (IC) * Cycles Per Instruction (CPI) * Clock Cycle Time','D'),(1223,49,'Identify the valid specification or operational behavior associated with JK Flip-Flop vs SR Flip-Flop:','SR Flip-Flop toggles when S=1 and R=1','D Flip-Flop has two inputs D1 and D2','T Flip-Flop cannot be used in binary counters','JK Flip-Flop eliminates the invalid/indeterminate state (S=1, R=1) by toggling the output when J=1 and K=1','D'),(1224,49,'Identify the valid specification or operational behavior associated with Multiplexer (2^n-to-1 MUX) and Decoder (n-to-2^n):','An 8-to-1 MUX requires 8 select lines','A 3-to-8 Decoder has 8 input lines and 3 output lines','Multiplexers are sequential memory elements','A 2^n-to-1 MUX selects 1 of 2^n data inputs using n select lines; an n-to-2^n Decoder activates 1 of 2^n outputs','D'),(1225,49,'Identify the valid specification or operational behavior associated with Memory-Mapped I/O vs Isolated (Port-Mapped) I/O:','Memory-Mapped I/O requires special IN and OUT assembly instructions','Isolated I/O reduces the available main memory address space','RISC architectures cannot use Memory-Mapped I/O','Memory-Mapped I/O shares the same address space and Load/Store instructions for both memory and I/O devices','D'),(1226,50,'During an evaluation of 2\'s Complement representation of signed integers, which option represents the standard behaviour or rule?',