'Both are stored on the hard disk','PC holds the result of ALU addition','IR holds the stack pointer address','A'),(1232,50,'During an evaluation of RISC vs CISC Instruction Set Architectures, which option represents the standard behaviour or rule?','RISC uses fixed-length instructions, load/store architecture, and many registers; CISC uses variable-length complex instructions','x86 is a pure RISC architecture','RISC allows arithmetic operations directly on memory operands','CISC cannot use instruction pipelining','A'),(1233,50,'During an evaluation of Immediate, Direct, Indirect, and Indexed Addressing Modes, which option represents the standard behaviour or rule?','Immediate: operand in instruction; Direct: address in instruction; Indirect: pointer in register/memory; Indexed: base + offset','Register mode is the slowest addressing mode','Immediate mode fetches the operand from disk','Direct mode requires two memory accesses to fetch the operand','A'),(1234,50,'During an evaluation of Carry-Lookahead Adder (CLA) vs Ripple-Carry Adder, which option represents the standard behaviour or rule?','CLA computes carry signals in parallel using Generate (G = AB) and Propagate (P = A xor B) to reduce propagation delay','CLA cannot add negative 2\'s complement numbers','Ripple-Carry Adder adds 64 bits in O(1) gate delay','CLA uses less hardware area than a Ripple-Carry Adder','A'),(1235,50,'During an evaluation of Booth\'s Multiplication Algorithm, which option represents the standard behaviour or rule?','Multiplies signed 2\'s complement numbers efficiently by encoding runs of 1s as a subtraction and addition','Uses division to compute products','Works only on unsigned positive integers','Requires converting numbers to BCD first','A'),(1236,50,'During an evaluation of Hardwired vs Microprogrammed Control Unit, which option represents the standard behaviour or rule?','Hardwired uses combinational logic/FSM (faster, RISC); Microprogrammed uses control memory storing microinst