lly Associative, and Set-Associative Cache, which option represents the standard behaviour or rule?','Direct-mapped: 1 block location (index = block mod N); Fully associative: any line; k-way Set-Associative: k lines per set','Set-associative cache cannot use LRU replacement','Direct-mapped cache has zero conflict misses','Fully associative cache requires no tag comparators','A'),(1242,50,'During an evaluation of Cache Write Policies (Write-Through vs Write-Back), which option represents the standard behaviour or rule?','Write-Through updates both cache and main memory on every write; Write-Back updates only cache (dirty bit) until eviction','Write-Back generates more memory bus traffic than Write-Through','Write-Back writes to main memory on every CPU store instruction','Write-Through requires a dirty bit per cache line','A'),(1243,50,'During an evaluation of Effective Memory Access Time (EMAT) formula, which option represents the standard behaviour or rule?','EMAT = Hit_Time + (Miss_Rate * Miss_Penalty)','EMAT is independent of the miss penalty','EMAT = Hit_Rate * Miss_Penalty','EMAT = Miss_Time / Hit_Rate','A'),(1244,50,'During an evaluation of Programmed I/O, Interrupt-Driven I/O, and Direct Memory Access (DMA), which option represents the standard behaviour or rule?','DMA transfers blocks directly between I/O device and memory via a DMA controller without continuous CPU intervention','Interrupt-Driven I/O has lower overhead than DMA for 1 GB disk transfers','Programmed I/O frees the CPU to run other processes while polling','DMA transfers data through CPU general-purpose registers on every byte','A'),(1245,50,'During an evaluation of Endianness (Big-Endian vs Little-Endian), which option represents the standard behaviour or rule?','Big-Endian stores the most significant byte (MSB) at the lowest memory address; Little-Endian stores the LSB at the lowest address','x86-64 processors are Big-Endian only','Little-Endian reverses the bits inside each individual byte'